From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai Krakow <kai@kaishome.de>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:38:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: pass the content type only for connectors that
 have it

The content type is passed to NVKMS when the device has a content type
property object, but DRM creates that object for the whole device as soon
as one connector attaches the property, and nvidia-drm attaches it to HDMI
connectors only. A connector without the property has a state value of 0,
"No Data", so every modeset on it sets NVKMS value 1 instead of 0, which
keeps the NVKMS default ("IT content, graphics"). NVKMS builds the AVI
InfoFrame for every HDMI display, including one behind a passive DP++
adapter or a DVI port, where user space cannot set the property. A TV that
is no longer told it shows IT content may pick a picture mode with more
video processing and latency.

Remember per connector whether the property was attached and pass the
content type only for those.

Not confirmed on hardware; found by reading the code.

Fixes: 5cbd792842e5 ("nvidia-drm: add the content type connector property")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c | 8 ++++++--
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.h | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c
index d8da3831..a9530884 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c
@@ -1023,9 +1023,11 @@ __nv_drm_connector_atomic_check(struct drm_connector *connector,
      * their page flip commits. Pass it with every modeset too, so it also
      * reaches a display that is newly driven by this CRTC or was recreated
      * by a hotplug. The DRM values are the NVKMS values minus one (NVKMS 0
-     * keeps its own default).
+     * keeps its own default). The property object exists for the whole
+     * device once one connector has it; a connector without it, such as an
+     * HDMI sink behind a DP++ adapter, keeps the NVKMS default.
      */
-    if ((connector->dev->mode_config.content_type_property != NULL) &&
+    if (to_nv_connector(connector)->has_content_type &&
         ((old_connector_state->content_type !=
           new_connector_state->content_type) ||
          drm_atomic_crtc_needs_modeset(crtc_state))) {
@@ -1261,6 +1263,8 @@ nv_drm_connector_new(struct drm_device *dev,
                 nv_dev,
                 "Failed to attach the content type property to connector created from physical index %u",
                 nv_connector->physicalIndex);
+        } else {
+            nv_connector->has_content_type = NV_TRUE;
         }
 
         if (nv_dev->nv_connector_hdmi_vsif_metadata_property) {
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.h b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.h
index 3ddc63bc..80e5006e 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.h
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.h
@@ -54,6 +54,9 @@ struct nv_drm_connector {
     NvBool internal;
     NvKmsConnectorType type;
 
+    /* The "content type" property is attached to this connector. */
+    NvBool has_content_type;
+
     char dpAddress[NVKMS_DP_ADDRESS_STRING_LENGTH];
 
     struct nv_drm_encoder *nv_detected_encoder;
